    "created_at": "2023-03-22T17:16:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-22T17:19:24Z",
    "body": "Ah I see. Thanks for the clarification!\r\n1. Are you suggesting that instead of `&key1=value1,value2`, it should (or better to) be `&key1=value1&key1=value2` by standard? Sorry I'm not familiar with this, so not sure how strict the requirement is to follow the latter format.\r\n2. Besides that, any suggestion on how to spec [EscapeQueryParamValue](https://crsrc.org/c/base/strings/escape.h;drc=b4bc946c63b2b95e1f05dec4e84adcadd10499c6;l=29) with its `use_plus` set to true? This is our [code](https://crsrc.org/c/content/services/auction_worklet/trusted_signals.cc;drc=d80a12e889e628c560d36a7346dc6934eadc07f1;l=41), if that's helpful. That is the part that I'm wondering how to document in our spec.\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
